# Copy to .env, fill in, and keep it out of version control.
# Prefer a token: it expires and can be revoked without changing your password.
# Generate one at https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/profile
#
# On your own computer, the simplest form is:
#   set EARTHDATA_TOKEN=paste-the-token-here     (Windows Command Prompt)
#   $env:EARTHDATA_TOKEN="paste-the-token-here"  (PowerShell)
#
# Do not pass the token as a command-line argument.

EARTHDATA_TOKEN=

# Alternative, less preferred:
# EARTHDATA_USERNAME=
# EARTHDATA_PASSWORD=

# On a shared Linux machine, a mode-600 file is better than an environment
# variable, because batch jobs do not always inherit your shell exports:
#   ~/.earthdata_token
#   ~/.netrc with: machine urs.earthdata.nasa.gov login YOUR_USER password YOUR_PASS
